          "media_absence_reason": "text_first_pilot",
          "media_role": "none",
          "narration": {
            "fact_ids": [
              "sec07-F07",
              "sec07-R05"
            ],
            "text": "Wearing a belt is not enough; fit decides protection. A correctly worn belt has a snug shoulder strap across shoulder and chest plus a lap portion low across the hips, fastened securely and never tucked under the arm or behind the back. The lap must sit on bone, not stomach, and the shoulder must stay centered. Check snugness, buckle click, and routing each time. Correct fit spreads force safely instead of injuring soft tissue."
          },
          "slide_id": "sec07-u03-s03",
          "title": {
            "fact_ids": [
              "sec07-F07"
            ],
            "text": "Fit Belt On Bone"
