          "narration": {
            "fact_ids": [
              "sec07-F11",
              "sec07-F14"
            ],
            "text": "Children and air bags demand precise rules, because small bodies face large forces. Every child age eight or younger must use an approved safety seat unless at fifty-seven inches, while air bags supplement belts rather than replacing them. This session walks the rear, forward, and booster stages, then rear seating and air-bag cooperation. Master the thresholds and placement rules, and you protect the most vulnerable riders on every single trip you make."
          },
          "slide_id": "sec07-u04-s01",
          "title": {
            "fact_ids": [
