              "text": "Gateway before all later stages."
            }
          ],
          "media_absence_reason": "text_first_pilot",
          "media_role": "none",
          "narration": {
            "fact_ids": [
              "sec07-F11",
              "sec07-R06"
            ],
            "text": "Start with the gateway that controls everything else. Every child age eight or younger must use an approved safety seat unless the child has reached fifty-seven inches in height. That age-or-height test decides whether you enter the staged sequence at all. Do not skip to adult belts early, even for tall-looking young children below the line. Confirm age and height first, then choose rear-facing, forward, or booster placement in the back seat."
          },
          "slide_id": "sec07-u04-s02",
          "title": {
            "fact_ids": [
              "sec07-F11"
            ],
            "text": "Gateway Age Height Rule"
          }
        },
        {
