          ],
          "media_absence_reason": "text_first_pilot",
          "media_role": "none",
          "narration": {
            "fact_ids": [
              "sec07-F12"
            ],
            "text": "The progression moves with growth, always in the back seat. Children ride rear-facing in the back seat to at least age two and thirty pounds, then forward-facing with a harness in the back seat to at least age four and forty pounds, then in a booster until the belt fits and they reach fifty-seven inches. Each stage matches size and strength to restraint design. Moving up early weakens protection, while staying through minimums keeps crash loads on the strongest structures and safest positions."
