          "narration": {
            "fact_ids": [
              "sec07-F13",
              "sec07-F15"
            ],
            "text": "Protection continues after boosters end. Children ages eight through twelve must use a suitable restraint or belt, and children age twelve or younger should keep riding in the back seat. Infants never ride in front of an active passenger air bag, and any child who must use an air-bag seat is moved fully rearward and properly secured. The back seat remains the safest place. Keep older children rearward and buckled even when they ask to move forward."
