          ],
          "media_absence_reason": "text_first_pilot",
          "media_role": "none",
          "narration": {
            "fact_ids": [
              "sec07-F14",
              "sec07-R10"
            ],
            "text": "Air bags are powerful partners, not soft cushions. Air bags supplement belts rather than replacing them, deploy from the dashboard at up to two hundred miles per hour, and protect best when occupants are buckled and children ride restrained in the back. That speed demands distance and buckling. Treat an air bag as a high-speed device that works with safety belts, and you gain combined protection instead of added injury risk for small occupants."
          },
          "slide_id": "sec07-u04-s05",
          "title": {
