            "text": "The two harness stages look alike, so separate them sharply. Keep a child rear-facing in the back seat until at least two years of age and thirty pounds, then keep a child forward-facing with a harness in the back seat until at least four years of age and forty pounds. Direction, age, and weight all shift together. Confusing them moves a toddler forward too soon. Hold rear-facing through its minimums before earning the forward-facing harness step in back."
